ADDRESS BOOK - C MINI PROJECT
=============================

Features
--------
* Add, list, search, update and delete contacts (CRUD).
* Up to five phone numbers and five email addresses per contact.
* Input validation for names, phone numbers and basic email syntax.
* Case-insensitive name/email search and phone substring search.
* Alphabetical sorting, database statistics and explicit save.
* CSV persistence with quoted fields (commas and quotes are supported).
* Automatic save after edits and append-only audit logging in ABK.LOG.
* Dynamic contact storage; no fixed maximum contact count.
* Optional data-file argument for working with a separate database.

Build
-----
From this directory run:
    make

Run
---
    ./abk
or:
    ./abk my_contacts.csv

The default data file is telephone.csv in the current working directory.
A missing data file starts as an empty address book and is created when saved.
The audit log is written to ABK.LOG in the current working directory.

CSV format
----------
Each row has 11 fields: name, five phone-number fields, and five email fields.
Fields are quoted and embedded quotes are doubled. Back up your CSV file before
editing it manually. If an existing CSV file is malformed, the program stops
rather than silently overwriting it.

Notes
-----
This is a small local console application; it does not encrypt contact details.
Keep the data file private and make backups of important contacts.
